{"call": "maker-1", "generation": {"cost_basis": "response-usage x pinned price", "data": {"provider_name": "deepseek-flash", "total_cost": 97486.95}}, "received_at": "2026-11-09T16:50:37.651831Z", "request": {"body": {"model": "deepseek-flash"}, "headers": {"Authorization": "Bearer [REDACTED]"}, "method": "POST", "url": "https://api.deepseek.com/beta/chat/completions"}, "response": {"choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "message": {"content": "Reading the failing bar, the defect is precise: `--allow-hand-times` currently suppresses the refusal for **every** entry in `hand`, including the entries `Call.hand_time_entries()` synthesises from a server `Date` header / `response.created` when the logger stamped nothing. Those are not hand-entered values, so the switch must not reach them. The no-switch path (which refuses them as `hand-time` and must stay byte-identical for A3a/A3b/T7b) is left alone; under the switch they become the `time` refusal the bar asks for, naming the log and **every** unstamped call.\n\nThe change is confined to `kit/emit_custody.py`: `evaluator_history()` gains `allow_hand` and, after `flag_calls`, refuses each unstamped evaluator call's synthesised entry with kind `time`. That is the same `Refusals` mechanism already used for \"a model evaluator with no harness log\", and it leaves maker logs, typed hand times, and every other refusal untouched. `kit/custody_history.py` needs no change \u2014 it already distinguishes the sources.\n\nkit/emit_custody.py\n````python\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\nswitch FLAGS hand times; it never verifies them, and it silences nothing else.\n=======\nswitch FLAGS hand times; it never verifies them, and it silences nothing else.\n\nThe switch is about times TYPED into the custody inputs, never an unsourced one. A model evaluator's check time\nthat exists only because its harness-log call carried no logger `sent_at`/`received_at`, so the reader fell back\nto a server `Date` header or a response `created` epoch, has