      f\"sent_at and received_at (tools/edi/or_call.py writes them).\")\n```\n\nWait \u2014 but the prompt says it must be refused under the switch, and not written. And also that D13 requires the record absent. Since ref non-empty \u21d2 exit 3.\n\nBut hold on \u2014 \"same refusal kind\" under the switch vs without? A1 asserts `[time]`. Without the switch the refusal kind is `[hand-time]`. The prompt's prose says same kind but the test says `[time]`. The tests are the spec. Fine.\n\nHmm, wait. Let me re-read A1:\n\n```python\nrc, out = emit(j14, o14, allow_hand=True)\nres((f\"{S} \u00b7 J14/A1 a model evaluator's check time is refused UNDER --allow-hand-times, naming the log \"\n     f\"(exit 3, [time], nothing written)\",\n     rc == 3 and \"[time]\" in out and \"harness-eval-a.log\" in out and not o14.exists(),\n     ...))\n```\n\nYes, `[time]`.\n\nBut careful: `out` here \u2014 does it already contain `[time]` from something else? j14 is `job_copy_raw(\"j14-boundary\")` + typed `passes.pass-a.at`. Under allow_hand, `passes.pass-a.at` is a typed hand time; under switch currently no refusal. Evaluator logs unstamped \u2192 with our change, refusals with `[time]`. Good.\n\nWait, but there's a subtlety: in j14 (the raw FIX copy plus typed pass at), is `pass-a` linked to a call? FIX's `pass-a` has `call` presumably. The cross_check with typed at and call at might exceed tolerance \u2192 currently a `[time]` refusal might already exist! That would explain why A1 could pass merely by... hmm, no. Currently under allow_hand, is there a `[time]` refusal already for j14? Let's think: `cross_check(ref, \"passes.pass-a.at\", f.get(\"at\"), call.at, ...)`. The typed value is \"2026-10-20T12:00:02Z\"; FIX's call for pass-a is at \"2026-10-20T12:00:03Z\" (per the E3 test mention \"harness-eval-a.log#...\" and T2 cases referencing 12:00:03Z). Delta 1s \u2192 within tolerance. So no `[time]` from cross_check. And A2 asserts `\"evaluator\" in out` \u2014 where would that come from? Our new message has `who` = \"evaluator eval-a\". Good. Also `harness-eval-a.log#` from the field.\n\nBut hmm \u2014 wait. The A1/A2 test run on j14 which is `job_copy_raw` + typed pass at. Since `job_copy_raw` uses FIX, its harness logs are unstamped. Under allow_hand=True, does any existing refusal fire? Let's check: typed pass at 12:00:02 vs call at 12:00:03 \u2192 fine. Also typed `passes.pass-a.at` marked as hand (`inputs-no-ledger`) \u2192 under allow_hand, admitted. So currently rc==0 \u2192 A1 red. With our change, refusals fire \u2192 rc 3, `[time]`, names log, \"evaluator\" \u2014 both A1/A2 green. \n\nNow also, are there other unstamped calls in FIX's evaluator log besides eval_artifact? A3a says `_EVAL_CALLS` from `harness-eval-a.log`; the six fields imply 3 calls. Each will get a `[time]` refusal. Fine.\n\nNow, must A1's `not o14.exists()` hold? main returns 3 without writing. Good.\n\nNow \u2014 but wait: there's a scene where `allow_hand` is True and the evaluator log is unstamped but the case expects rc 0. Which green cases could that be?\n\nLet's enumerate all `emit(..., allow_hand=True)` calls (the default) that expect rc == 0 and where the evaluator's harness log might be unstamped:\n\n- All the job_copy(...) based success cases: LOGGED is stamped. Unless an overlay replaces the evaluator log with an unstamped one.\n- `j14b = job_copy_logged(\"j14-hand-only\")` \u2014 stamped.\n- `TJ` tool-built \u2014 `stamp_log` applied to all harness-*.log. Good.\n- `emit(LOGGED, rec_path)` etc.\n- `F1h` case `job_copy(\"f1h\")` (LOGGED) adding ledger events \u2192 stamped.\n- `X1` job_copy(\"x1-inputs\") \u2192 stamped.\n- `same-family` job_copy \u2192 stamped.\n- `no-inputs` \u2192 custody deleted.\n- `live-match` job_copy \u2192 stamped.\n- `agent-adopted` \u2192 stamped.\n- `tol59` \u2192 job_copy_logged \u2192 stamped.\n- pin success cases:\n  - `emit(j, TMP / \"unpinned.json\")` on `job_copy(\"pin-unpinned\", \"routing-unpinned\")` expects rc == 1 (hard gap, record written). LOGGED base \u2192 evaluator log stamped unless overlay replaces. The overlay \"routing-unpinned\" is about the request body, likely replaces the maker log's `request` field to drop the `provider` object. If it replaces the maker log (with `json.dumps(x)` after editing) \u2014 `shared`? Let's look: for pin-deny etc. they edit the maker log in place. Overlays in `tests/fixtures/custody/failures/routing-unpinned` presumably contain a modified harness-maker log. If that modified log lacks sent_at/received_at, our new refusal (which we're only applying to evaluators) won't touch the maker. Good \u2014 sticking to evaluators only avoids this.\n  - Are there overlay fixtures that modify the *evaluator* log for success cases? Possibly \"pin-*\" overlays modify the maker log only (maker pins). Likely fine.\n  - `pin-deny`: edits maker log in place. Fine.\n  - `pin-nobody`: edits maker log. Expects rc == 1. Fine.\n  - `same/json`, etc.\n\n- `emit(FIX, TMP / \"t3c.json\", allow_hand=True)` in the T3 sub-case: `emit(job_copy(\"t3-contradiction\", \"hand-times\"), TMP / \"t3c.json\", allow_hand=True)[0] == 3`. Expects 3 \u2014 our change might add refusals; still 3. Fine.\n\n- d15 in test_evaluator_harness_log.py:\n\n```python\ndef test_d15_switch_admits_a_genuine_hand_entered_time(self):\n    job = self._job(json.dumps(self.GOOD) + \"\\n\")\n    p = job / \"inputs\" / \"custody.json\"\n    c = json.loads(p.read_text())\n    c[\"passes\"][\"dim1#p1\"][\"at\"] = \"2026-11-08T10:00:06Z\"   # typed: no ledger line behind it\n    p.write_text(json.dumps(c))\n    r = self._emit(job, allow_hand_times=True)\n    rec = self._record(job)\n    self.assertIsNotNone(rec, ...)\n    ...\n    self.assertEqual((rec[\"predicate\"][\"checks\"][0]).get(\"at\"), \"2026-11-08T10:00:09Z\", ...)\n```\n\nHere `GOOD` has sent_at/received_at stamped. So no server-header entries. Under switch, typed `at` admitted \u2192 record written; check at = GOOD.received_at 10:00:09Z. Our ch