-time\", f\"{e['field']} {e['file']}:{e['line']} ({e['source']})\")\n=======\n    xp[\"schema\"] = \"plumbline/x-plumbline/v1\"\n    xp[\"hand_times\"] = [hand[k] for k in hand]\n    if hand and allow_hand:\n        xp[\"allowances\"] = {\"hand_times\": {\"switch\": \"--allow-hand-times\", \"writer\": emitter_stamp(),\n                                           \"at\": H.iso(now)}}\n        # The switch is about a value TYPED into the custody inputs with no ledger line behind it. It is not a\n        # licence for a model evaluator's check time the logger never stamped: that time exists only because the\n        # reader fell back to the response `Date` header or the response `created` epoch, and a record carrying it\n        # would report a check time with no logger source (the hollow record this program has shipped before).\n        # Refused with kind `time`, naming the log and EVERY call it did not stamp -- not aborted at the first --\n        # so the refusal cannot be satisfied by the abort-at-first-entry regression (Job 14;\n        # docs/custody-emission.md, Refusals: `[time]` is a check time with no logger source).\n        for who, entry in ev_unsourced:\n            basis = (\"response Date header\" if entry[\"source\"] == \"server-header\"\n                     else \"response created epoch\")\n            ref.add(\"time\", f\"{who}: {entry['field']} carries no logger sent_at/received_at, so its time would be \"\n                            f\"the {basis} at {entry['file']}:{entry['line']} ({entry['source']}). \"\n                            f\"--allow-hand-times admits a time TYPED into the custody inputs with no ledger line \"\n                            f\"behind it; it does not admit a model evaluator's check time the logger never stamped \"\n                            f\"(custody CL1-15). Re-run the call so the logger records sent_at/received_at.\")\n    if hand and not allow_hand:\n        for e in hand.values():\n            ref.add(\"hand-time\", f\"{e['field']} {e['file']}:{e['line']} ({e['source']})\")\n>>>>>>> REPLACE\n````\n\nWhat each block does:\n\n1. `flag_calls()` now returns the entries it added, so `evaluator_history()` can report every unstamped call without changing `hand_time_entries()` or the emitted `hand_times[]` shape.\n2. `evaluator_history()` keeps those entries in a separate list (`unsourced`), on both return paths.\n3. `build()` aggregates them per model evaluator.\n4. The assembly block refuses them **only when `--allow-hand-times` is on**, with kind `time` and a message naming `evaluator <id>`, the field (`<log>#<call>.sent_at` / `.received_at`), the file:line and the source. The no-switch path is untouched, so its `hand-time` refusal is unchanged.\n\n`kit/custody_history.py` needs no change: `Call.hand_time_entries()` already distinguishes a server-derived time (`server-header` / `response-created`) from a typed one (`inputs-no-ledger` / `ledger-hand` / `ledger-no-writer`), which is exactly the distinction the bar draws.\n\nI cannot run the two commands in this environment, so here is the reading I expect from the change, case by case:\n\n- **Yours, expected green**: `J14/A1` (exit 3, `[time]`, `harness-eval-a.log`, nothing written), `J14/A2` (message names `evaluator` and `harness-eval-a.log#<call>`), `test_d13_switch_does_not_admit_an_unsourced_evaluator_time` (exit \u2260 0, `harness-eval.log`, no record), `test_d14_switch_refusal_names_every_unstamped_call` (all of `dim1#p1/p2/p3` and `.sent_at`).\n- **Must stay green and untouched by this diff**: `J14/A3a`, `J14/A3b`, `J14/A4`, `T7b/E3`, `V1/V3/T2`, `T3`, `E2`, and the other 13 evaluator-harness-log tests \u2014 none of them reaches the new branch: `A3a/A3b/T7b-E3` run with no switch (the `hand and not allow_hand` branch, unchanged), and `A4/T3/E2/V1` run on logger-stamped logs, so `ev_unsourced` is empty.\n- **Other jobs' reds**: the 59 s case, `T2c`, `T3`'s switch case and `E2` are not touched (the new refusal fires only when `ev_unsourced` is non-empty, i.e. a model evaluator logged a call with no logger `sent_at`/`received_at`).\n- **One honest caveat you should adjudicate**: the case in `tests/validate_schemas.py` that emits the `job-rejected` fixture with the switch on and expects `exit 3, [time], \u2026 \"harness\"` is the *same phenomenon* as `J14/A1`, because `j14-boundary` is a raw copy of that fixture. If that case is the one you listed as a \"line-609 red\", this change will turn it green as a consequence of the behaviour the bar requires; no extra code targets it, and I did not add anything to reach it. If you would rather it stay red, that needs a different fixture surface, not a different emitter rule.", "function_call": null, "provider_specific_fields": {"reasoning_content": "Let me understand the task. The issue: under `--allow-hand-times`, a model evaluator's unsourced check time (server header / response created, i.e. `server-header` / `response-created` sources) is admitted. It must be refused regardless of the switch. Genuine hand times (`inputs-no-ledger`, `ledger-hand`, `ledger-no-writer`) are admitted under the switch and listed.\n\nLook at the code. In `build()`:\n\n```python\n    xp[\"hand_times\"] = [hand[k] for k in hand]\n    if hand and allow_hand:\n        xp[\"allowances\"] = {\"hand_times\": {\"switch\": \"--allow-hand-times\", \"writer\": emitter_stamp(),\n                                           \"at\": H.iso(now)}}\n    if hand and not allow_hand:\n        for e in hand.values():\n            ref.add(\"hand-time\", f\"{e['field']} {e['file']}:{e['line']} ({e['source']})\")\n```\n\nSo the entries in `hand` have `source` of kinds: `inputs-no-ledger`, `ledger-hand`, `ledger-no-writer`, `server-header`, `response-created` (from `Call.hand_time_entries()`).\n\nThe requirement: the switch must only admit hand times whose source is a typed/ledger hand time. Unsourced model-evaluator times (server-header/response-created) must ALWAYS be refused with kind `time`, naming the harness log and naming EVERY unstamped call.\n\nLet me check the failing test expectations in `tests/test_evaluator_harness_log.py`:\n\nD13: under `--allow-hand-times` with `UNSTAMPED` log entry: refusal, exit nonzero, output contains `harness-eval.log`, and no record written.\n\nD14: three unstamped calls, all named `dim1#p1`, `dim1#p2`, `dim1#p3`, and `.sent_at` in output.\n\nWait \u2014 the job they build in `_job` includes `harness_log: \"custody/evidence/harness-eval.log\"`, and log content is `UNSTAMPED` entries: `{\"call\": \"dim1#p1\", \"request\": {...}, \"response\": {\"model\": \"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash\"}, \"response_headers\": {\"Date\": \"Sun, 08 Nov 2026 10:00:09 GMT\"}}`. So no sent_at/received_at, but a Date header. `Call.sent` is None -> source `server-header`. Actually `self.created` is None, `self.date` set. So `hand_time_entries` yields entries for `sent_at` (server-header) and `received_at` (server-header). So the field names look like `harness-eval.log#dim1#p1.sent_at` \u2014 and test D14 asserts `f\"dim1#p{n}\"` in out and `.sent_at` in out. And the refusal must be `[time]`? A1 asserts `\"[time]\" in out` and `\"harness-eval-a.log\" in out`. Hmm, A1 test uses a job from `job_copy_raw(\"j14-boundary\")` \u2014 the fixture's harness log `harness-eval-a.log`, with server times only. Under `--allow-hand-times`, expects exit 3, `[time]` in out, `harness-eval-a.log` in out, and no record. But wait, the emitted refusal from `ref` \u2014 since `ref` nonempty causes exit 3 and prints each as `  [{kind}] {msg}`. Currently under allow_hand, `hand` exists so allowance recorded, and since `allow_hand` no hand-time refusals added. But the fixture would presumably be refused for something else? Let's think: the fixture `job_copy_raw` = copy of `FIX` (job-rejected) without stamping, with typed pass at. Under switch... would emit. But A1 expects refusal.\n\nSo we need to add a refusal when there is a hand time whose source is a server-derived time for a model evaluator. Kind `time` (per A1's `[time]`). Message must name the log `harness-eval-a.log`.\n\nFor D13, the message must contain `harness-eval.log` (the log file name). D14 must name all three calls and `.sent_at`. If we name each entry's field `harness-eval.log#dim1#p1.sent_at`, that satisfies both.\n\nBut wait: how do we distinguish \"model evaluator's\" entries from the maker's? The requirement says: \"It is not a licence to admit an unsourced model-evaluator check time\". So only evaluator-origin server times must be refused; the maker's server times can be allowed under the switch? Hmm. Actually let's read the bar carefully.\n\nA3a: \"the no-switch refusal names EVERY evaluator call the log carries\" \u2014 that's no switch, so the `hand-time` refusal lists all calls. A3b: the no-switch refusal publishes all six evaluator hand_time fields. So under no-switch, currently `flag_calls` marks each and `hand and not allow_hand` adds `hand-time` per entry. Good, currently passing.\n\nA4: `job_copy_logged` (logger-stamped logs) + typed pass time under switch \u2192 exit 0, hand_times listed. Good.\n\nD13/D14: `harness-eval.log` for evaluator. Under switch, must refuse with `[time]` naming the log and each call.\n\nSo the fix: the server-derived hand times on a MODEL EVALUATOR (and probably also maker?) must always be refused as `time`. The prompt says \"an **unsourced model-evaluator check time**\". Let me be conservative: the check time of a model evaluator. But actually the general principle: the switch is about hand-typed values, not server-synthesised times. Hmm, but should we refuse the maker's server time under the switch too? A4's job_copy_logged stamps everything, so no maker server times remain. T3 in validate_schemas: `emit(LOGGED, o, allow_hand=True)` \u2014 LOGGED has stamped logs. So not affected. E2: job_copy_logged again. Not affected.\n\nThe prompt says: \"It is **not** a licence to admit an **unsourced model-evaluator check time**\". So c