tor whose harness log carries no logger times is refused, naming the log (exit 3, [time], nothing written)\" \u2014 wait, that case expects `[time]` in out already! Let me look).\n\nIn validate_schemas.py:\n\n```python\no_ref = TMP / \"fixture-refused.json\"\nrc, out = emit(FIX, o_ref)\nres((f\"{S} \u00b7 a model evaluator whose harness log carries no logger times is refused, naming the log \"\n     f\"(exit 3, [time], nothing written)\",\n     rc == 3 and \"[time]\" in out and \"harness\" in out and not o_ref.exists(),\n     f\"exit {rc}: {out.strip()[-140:]}\"))\n```\n\nHmm, that's the \"line-609 `[time]` refusal case\" that is RED and belongs to other jobs? The prompt says: \"Five reds in `tests/validate_schemas.py` belong to **other jobs**. Do not attempt them and do not make them green: the line-609 `[time]` refusal case, ...\". Hmm interesting \u2014 so that case currently red, and we must not make it green. Wait but if we add `[time]` refusals for evaluator server times, we might make this case green. Let me re-read: \"Five reds ... belong to other jobs. Do not attempt them and do not make them green: the line-609 `[time]` refusal case, the 'hand time 59 s off' case, `T2c`, `T3`'s switch case, and `E2`.\"\n\nHmm. So line-609 case is red currently and must remain red? That seems weird. Let me look: `emit(FIX, o_ref)` where `emit()` defaults `allow_hand=True`. Wait:\n\n```python\ndef emit(job, out, tree=None, extra=(), allow_hand=True):\n    \"\"\"...\"\"\"\n    args = [...]\n    if allow_hand:\n        args.append(\"--allow-hand-times\")\n```\n\nSo `emit(FIX, o_ref)` passes `--allow-hand-times`! So under the switch, FIX's logs unstamped \u2192 currently written (maybe with gaps) \u2192 case red. Under our change, refusals for evaluator server times \u2192 exit 3, and the message must contain `[time]` and `harness`. Then this case would turn GREEN. But the prompt says do not make it green... Hmm. But maybe it's red for a different reason and would stay red? Let